export const NODE_OPERATORS = {"html": "<h1 id=\"node-operators\">Node Operators</h1>\n<p>A Nexus node is a self-hosted machine that joins the federated Nexus Systems\nnetwork. Node operators contribute storage and bandwidth to the network and in\nreturn run a full, sovereign copy of the platform on hardware they control.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-a-node-does\">What a node does</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Hosts Nexus applications for users on that node</li>\n<li>Participates in federated routing — sites and mail can replicate across peers</li>\n<li>Holds an Ed25519 cryptographic identity that peers use to verify its messages</li>\n<li>Appears in the network's public node directory at <code>GET /api/v1/nodes</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"what-you-need\">What you need</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Requirement</th>\n<th>Minimum</th>\n<th>Notes</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Machine</td>\n<td>Raspberry Pi 4 / small VPS</td>\n<td>Must stay online to serve traffic</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Domain</td>\n<td>Any resolvable hostname</td>\n<td>e.g. <code>node.example.com</code> — used as the node's identity</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Storage</td>\n<td>1 GB</td>\n<td>Declared at enrollment; more is better</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Bandwidth</td>\n<td>1 GB/month</td>\n<td>Declared at enrollment</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Network</td>\n<td>Outbound port 443</td>\n<td>Inbound is optional (tunnel mode works without it)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>OS</td>\n<td>Linux</td>\n<td>The install script is a shell script; Bun is installed automatically</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>You do not need a routable public IP. Cloudflare Tunnel or any other reverse\nproxy that terminates TLS for your domain works.</p>\n<h2 id=\"enrollment-flow\">Enrollment flow</h2>\n<p>Enrollment happens in two steps. The split is intentional: this server never\nsees your private key.</p>\n<h3 id=\"step-1-register-requires-a-tnhcdev-account\">Step 1 — Register (requires a tnhc.dev account)</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Sign in at <code>https://app.tnhc.dev</code>.</li>\n<li>Go to <strong>Node Operators</strong> (<code>app.tnhc.dev/node-operators</code>) and click\n   <strong>Enroll a node</strong>, or go directly to <code>app.tnhc.dev/cloud/federation</code>.</li>\n<li>Fill in your node's name, domain, region, and declared capacities.</li>\n<li>You receive an <strong>enrollment token</strong> — a single-use, 24-hour secret. Copy it\n   immediately; it is not stored in a recoverable form.</li>\n<li>You also receive a ready-to-run install command, e.g.:</li>\n</ol>\n<p><code>sh\n   curl -fsSL https://hosting.tnhc.dev/install-node.sh -o install-node.sh \\\n     &amp;&amp; sh install-node.sh --token &lt;your-token&gt; --api https://hosting.tnhc.dev</code></p>\n<h3 id=\"step-2-claim-runs-on-your-machine-no-account-needed\">Step 2 — Claim (runs on your machine, no account needed)</h3>\n<p>Run the install command on the machine that will be the node. The script:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Generates an Ed25519 keypair locally — the private key never leaves your machine.</li>\n<li>Signs the enrollment token with the private key.</li>\n<li>Calls <code>POST /nodes/claim</code> with the token, your public key, and the signature.</li>\n<li>The server verifies the signature, registers the public key, and activates your node.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Your node moves from <code>pending</code> → <code>active</code>. From this point peers can discover\nand verify it by its registered public key.</p>\n<h3 id=\"if-the-token-expires\">If the token expires</h3>\n<p>Tokens expire after 24 hours. If you miss the window, ask an operator to revoke\nthe old token (<code>POST /nodes/:id/enrollment/revoke</code>) and issue a new enrollment.</p>\n<h2 id=\"regions\">Regions</h2>\n<p>Use a short geographic slug that describes where the machine sits, e.g.\n<code>eu-north</code>, <code>eu-west</code>, <code>us-east</code>, <code>us-west</code>, <code>ap-southeast</code>. The value is\ninformational — routing decisions are not based on it today — but it helps\noperators understand the network's topology.</p>\n<h2 id=\"after-enrollment\">After enrollment</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Your node appears in <code>GET /api/v1/nodes</code> (public federation directory).</li>\n<li>Federation peers will discover and attempt to connect to your node.</li>\n<li>The Cloud console at <code>app.tnhc.dev/cloud/federation</code> shows the network's\n  current peer list and trust status.</li>\n<li>The node's last-seen timestamp is updated on each successful handshake.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"api-reference\">API reference</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Endpoint</th>\n<th>Auth</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>GET /nodes</code></td>\n<td>None</td>\n<td>Public federation directory</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>POST /nodes/enroll</code></td>\n<td>Session</td>\n<td>Start enrollment; returns single-use token</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>POST /nodes/claim</code></td>\n<td>Token (not session)</td>\n<td>Finish enrollment with public key + signature</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>POST /nodes/:id/enrollment/revoke</code></td>\n<td>Session</td>\n<td>Revoke an unclaimed token</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Base URL: <code>https://hosting.tnhc.dev</code></p>\n<h2 id=\"questions\">Questions</h2>\n<p>Open an issue at <code>github.com/The-No-Hands-Company/Nexus-Systems</code> or reach out\ndirectly. Running even a temporary node on a small VPS helps stress-test the\nfederation protocol — it is appreciated.</p>", "source": "https://github.com/The-No-Hands-company/Nexus-Systems/blob/main/docs/NODE-OPERATORS.md", "commit": "b1164a1236253ad020ebcf0f39d696f81939ab2b"};
